I have a complete picture of the current owner-identity implementation. Here is my thorough report.

## Overview

This is a Spring PetClinic ("PetClinic-Evolve") project with an OfficeFloor-style create pipeline. Owner identity fields are computed by small single-responsibility function classes under `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`, wired together by `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`, and surfaced on the DTO via MapStruct expressions in `OwnerMapper`.

There is an important signal that a **redesign is expected**: the sole active acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) and its docstring say `customerCode` must **become** `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, whereas the current code produces `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'`. The OpenAPI doc yet again describes a third format `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'`. These three do not agree today.

Create pipeline order (from `owners.POST.yml`): build → validatePostcode → normalizeAddress → normalizeTelephone → normalizeEmail → rejectDuplicateIdentity → rejectCityAtCapacity → rejectDailyLimit → **assignCustomerCode** → **save** (audit) → respond.

---

## 1. customerCode building (current format with sequence number)

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`
**Class:** `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` — 3 methods (`service`, `prefix`, `cityCount`).

Format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`; NNNN is a per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence = (owners already in that city) + 1. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner is not yet counted (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`).

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String city3 = prefix(owner.getCity());
    String last3 = prefix(owner.getLastName());
    int sequence = cityCount(owner.getCity(), ownerRepository) + 1;
    owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence));
}
private static String prefix(String value) {
    return value.substring(0, Math.min(3, value.length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
private static int cityCount(String city, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    return (int) ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .filter(existing -> city.equals(existing.getCity()))
        .count();
}
```

Note: the class Javadoc says `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and matches the code. But `openapi.yml` (line 2090-2094) describes `customerCode` as `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` example `'SMI-0007'` — an inconsistency with the implementation.

Field storage — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (class `Owner extends Person`): `@Column(name = "customer_code") private String customerCode;` with `getCustomerCode()`/`setCustomerCode()`.

---

## 2. Membership number and its check digit (derived from customerCode)

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`
**Class/interface:** `OwnerMapper` (MapStruct `@Mapper`) — the interface declares ~6 mapping methods plus 1 default method. The identity derivations are MapStruct `@Mapping` expressions on `toOwnerDto`:

```java
@Mapping(target = "householdId", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.HouseholdId.of(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.IdentityKey.of(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
@Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.CheckDigit.of(owner))")
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
```

- **membershipNumber** = `customerCode + "-M" + <YY>` where YY = last two digits of `registrationDate.getYear()` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`). Depends on `registrationDate` being non-null (set in `BuildOwner`).
- **checkDigit** delegates to `CheckDigit.of(owner)`.

**Check digit file:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckDigit.java`
**Class:** `CheckDigit` (final, private ctor) — 1 public method `of` plus private ctor. Single **Luhn** check digit over the digits in `customerCode`, ignoring non-digit separators:

```java
public static int of(Owner owner) {
    String code = owner.getCustomerCode();
    int sum = 0;
    boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = code.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = code.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') { continue; }
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) { d -= 9; } }
        sum += d;
        dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

