## 3. Create audit record

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/SaveOwner.java`
**Class:** `SaveOwner` — 1 method (`service`). Persists then logs to a dedicated `AUDIT` SLF4J logger:

```java
private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}", owner.getId(),
        owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
}
```

The audit message format is exactly `owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}`. This is asserted in tests via the `AUDIT` logger capture helper (see section 7).

---

## 4. Locality derivation

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Locality.java`
**Class:** `Locality` (final, private ctor) — 2 methods (`of`, `fromPostcode`). Postcode takes precedence over the city table; falls back to `UNKNOWN`.

```java
private static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(
        "Sydney", "NSW", "Melbourne", "VIC", "Brisbane", "QLD");

public static String of(Owner owner) {
    String byPostcode = fromPostcode(owner.getPostcode());
    if (byPostcode != null) { return byPostcode; }
    return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(owner.getCity(), "UNKNOWN");
}

private static String fromPostcode(String postcode) {
    if (postcode == null || !postcode.matches("\\d{4}")) { return null; }
    int code = Integer.parseInt(postcode);
    if (code >= 2000 && code <= 2099) { return "NSW"; }
    if (code >= 3000 && code <= 3099) { return "VIC"; }
    if (code >= 4000 && code <= 4099) { return "QLD"; }
    return null;
}
```

Locality is set on the read DTO in `RespondWithOwner.service` via `dto.setLocality(Locality.of(owner))` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwner.java`). Note the create response (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) does **not** set locality.

---

## 5. Postcode / region code derivation and validation

**Region ranges (validation):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`
**Class:** `ValidateOwnerPostcode` — 1 method (`service`). Optional postcode; when present must be 4 digits and, for a city with a known region (via `Locality.of`), within that region's range. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode. Invalid → 400 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.

```java
private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_RANGE = Map.of(
        "NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099}, "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});

public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    if (postcode == null) { return; }
    int[] range = REGION_RANGE.get(Locality.of(owner));
    if (!postcode.matches("[0-9]{4}")
            || (range != null && (Integer.parseInt(postcode) < range[0] || Integer.parseInt(postcode) > range[1]))) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("postcode"));
    }
}
```

The region→range mapping also appears in `fromPostcode` inside `Locality.java` (section 4), and is documented at `openapi.yml` line 2040-2042. The three regions/ranges: NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099.

---

## 6. Telephone normalization / SHA-256 / hashing logic

**E.164 telephone normalization:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`
**Class:** `E164Telephone` (package-private final, private ctor) — 1 method (`toE164`). Keeps leading `+`/country code; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets; returns null unless 8-15 digits after `+`, with `+61`⇒9 national digits and `+1`⇒10.

```java
static String toE164(String raw) {
    if (raw == null) { return null; }
    boolean international = raw.trim().startsWith("+");
    String digits = raw.replaceAll("\\D", "");
    if (!international) {
        if (digits.startsWith("0")) { digits = digits.substring(1); }
        digits = "61" + digits;
    }
    if (digits.length() < 8 || digits.length() > 15) { return null; }
    if (digits.startsWith("61") && digits.length() != 2 + 9) { return null; }
    if (digits.startsWith("1") && digits.length() != 1 + 10) { return null; }
    return "+" + digits;
}
```

Applied in-place by `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.service` (`/home/daniel/.../NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`, class `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, 1 method); rejects 400 when result is null.

**SHA-256 hashing (householdId):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdId.java`
**Class:** `HouseholdId` (final, private ctor) — 2 methods (`of`, `normalize`). Key = normalized(lastName) + ' ' + normalized(address); normalization = trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase. SHA-256 of UTF-8 bytes, first 8 bytes rendered as **16 upper-case hex chars**:

```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    String key = normalize(owner.getLastName()) + ' ' + normalize(owner.getAddress());
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(key.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder id = new StringBuilder(16);
        for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) { id.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i])); }
        return id.toString();
    } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException ex) { throw new IllegalStateException(ex); }
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```

**identityKey (duplicate detection):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/IdentityKey.java`
**Class:** `IdentityKey` (final, private ctor) — 3 methods (`of`, `telephone`, `email`). Key = `E164Telephone(tel) + '|' + lowercased-email-or-empty + '|' + HouseholdId.of(owner)`.

```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    return telephone(owner) + '|' + email(owner) + '|' + HouseholdId.of(owner);
}
static String telephone(Owner owner) {
    String telephone = E164Telephone.toE164(owner.getTelephone());
    return telephone == null ? "" : telephone;
}
static String email(Owner owner) {
    String email = owner.getEmail();
    return (email == null || email.isBlank()) ? "" : email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```

Consumed by `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity` (`/home/daniel/.../RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`, class `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`, 1 method) which throws 409 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` on a telephone+email collision.

Related normalizers (context): `NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` (class `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, 1 method — optional, lowercases, regex `^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`), and `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java`.

---

## 7. Tests (unit/acceptance) and expected values

All tests live under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`. There are **no** dedicated JUnit unit tests for these functions — only the acceptance suite (three files). Testing is black-box over `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

**A. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`**
Class `AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase` — 1 test. The class Javadoc states the **redesign target**: `"global-id: Redesign owner identity. The customerCode must become '<REGION>-<HASH8>' where REGION is t..."`. The test asserts the NEW target format (regex `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`), which the current `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` does not produce:

```java
@Test
void coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(withPostcode(ownerNode()));
    JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
    assertTrue(n.get("customerCode").asText().matches("[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}")); // <REGION>-<HASH8>
}
```

**B. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`**
Abstract class `AcceptanceBase` — ~25 helper methods. `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username = "acceptance-admin", roles = {"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`.

Pinned ground-truth reference data (expected values):

```java
