Note: `sha256hex` produces **lower**-case full hex, `shaHex(s,n)` uppercases the first n chars (matching a `<HASH8>` upper-case expectation). Production `HouseholdId` uses upper-case (`%02X`) first 8 bytes = 16 chars; the redesign target `<HASH8>` implies 8 upper-case hex chars.

